{
  "title": "Insta360 GO Ultra latch mount on a cold shoe",
  "summary": "A printed version of the official Quick Release Mount's principle: two hooks click into the latch slots under the GO Ultra's Action Pod, release buttons at both ends, GoPro prongs underneath, on a cold-shoe foot with a lock wheel. Nothing touches the screen, buttons, ports or lens.",
  "status": "preview",
  "date": "2026-11-26",
  "material": "PLA (base, prongs, mount hardware: TNT, 0.12 mm, 6 walls, 60 % gyroid) + TPU 95A (sponge pad: Gås)",
  "notes": "Holds the pod the way Insta360's own mount does: by the two latch slots in the pod's bottom. Each hook sits on a PLA spring arm printed in one piece with the base (joined only at the front); a rigid arm runs from each spring to a ridged button outside the pod's end, and a hard stop limits the travel (1.8 mm, 1.3 % strain). The hooks' flat catches point outward under the slots' outer rims, so the pod can't come off until both buttons are squeezed. A TPU sponge pad (sparse gyroid, glued into the base) pushes the pod up against the catches: no rattle for a catch depth anywhere from 0.9 to 2.4 mm. Pod on: press it down until both hooks click (about 20 N). Pod off: squeeze both buttons and lift. Everything sits below the pod's bottom except the two hooks: the screen flips freely and the shutter, power, Q, USB-C, release slider, speaker, mics, lens and lights are untouched. A slot under the pod's lanyard hole lets the included safety cord loop round the base. Mount: cold-shoe foot in two widths (keep the snug one), knurled lock wheel, 3-prong head on a square key (forward/sideways/back) with the M5 thumbscrew; the base's prong block (glued into its bottom pocket) sits between the head's prongs, so the pod tilts. Checked in verify_mount.py: 20 of 21 targets pass. Not knowable without the camera: how deep the latch holes are. The hook tips reach 3.3 mm into them (4.3 mm while pressing the pod down); if the holes are shallower, the hooks need shortening. When the camera arrives: measure the hole depth and the catch with the workbench caliper first. Slot positions and sizes come from a photo of an empty pod's bottom scaled by its 70.4 mm width (+-0.6 mm); the hooks tolerate that. Plates: TNT, PLA at 230 C / 12 mm3/s, 1 h 55 min, 27 g, no supports. Gås, TPU sponge, 5 min, 1.5 g (1 wall, 2 top/bottom layers, 20 % gyroid). Assembly: superglue the sponge into the top pocket and the prong block into the bottom pocket.",
